WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Schedule, start and complete work on a job.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.800
Open the job. Work items live on the job. Let's open one.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:17.567
Work items. One item per estimate section and per approved change order, each with its own crew, crew-hours and days.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:21.933
Add work. For extra work that is not on the estimate.

00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:26.500
What. Say what the work is, e.g. Extra steps.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.167
Crew-hours. The hours the crew needs in total. The board turns them into days using the crew's hours a day.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:39.233
Crew. Who does it. You can leave it and pick the crew when you schedule it.

00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:46.100
Add it. Add puts it on the job and in the "To schedule" list on the board. The tour doesn't press it.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:51.267
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

00:00:51.767 --> 00:01:00.300
One work item. Crew colour, the name, work order number, crew, crew-hours, hours the crew logged and photos, then its status.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:09.667
Its days. The days it is booked. A red "over" day means the crew has more hours than it can do that day: move this or the other work.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:15.633
Reopen. On a finished item: puts it back in progress when the crew has to go back.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:25.667
Complete. Marks the item done. When the last item is done the job turns Complete, ready to invoice. The crew lead can also do it on the phone.

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:32.333
Materials. Click Materials to see what this item needs. A tick means the crew loaded it.

00:01:32.833 --> 00:01:40.300
Reschedule. Opens the schedule form for this item. On an item not on the board yet the button says Schedule.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.400
Crew. Pick the crew; each shows its speciality.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.667
Start day. The first day on site.

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:55.433
Budgeted crew-hours. The hours budgeted. The days are these hours ÷ the crew's hours a day.

00:01:55.933 --> 00:02:02.367
Or set the days. Leave 0 to work the days out from the hours, or type the number of days.

00:02:02.867 --> 00:02:10.233
The days it takes. A preview of the days. Weekends are skipped unless the job works them (Working days card).

00:02:10.733 --> 00:02:15.167
Take it off the board. Puts the item back in the To schedule list.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:23.433
Book the days. Schedule books it and tells you if the crew goes over capacity on any day. The tour doesn't press it.

00:02:23.933 --> 00:02:28.600
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:36.667
Not on the board yet. An item with no days says "Not on the schedule yet" and has a Schedule button: the same form.

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:44.600
Remove an item. The bin removes an item that has not started (it asks first). It comes off the schedule too.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:51.833
Crew note. A note for the crew on this item, from the estimate or a change order. It shows on their phone.

00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:57.600
Open the job. Now a job that is booked but not started, to see Start.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:07.800
Start. Marks the item in progress (the crew lead usually does it on the phone). A job on Permit hold shows a red tag instead and can't start.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:13.900
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
